  "captions": [
    {
      "text": "Imagine a monster tsunami racing toward New",
      "start": 0.2,
      "end": 2.512
    },
    {
      "text": "York City.",
      "start": 2.512,
      "end": 3.035
    },
    {
      "text": "Manhattan underwater.",
      "start": 3.075,
      "end": 4.24
    },
    {
      "text": "The Statue of Liberty surrounded by",
      "start": 4.316,
      "end": 5.711
    },
    {
      "text": "raging waves.",
      "start": 5.711,
      "end": 6.616
    },
    {
      "text": "Could this nightmare actually happen?",
      "start": 6.656,
      "end": 8.279
    },
    {
      "text": "Here’s the terrifying part:",
      "start": 8.729,
      "end": 10.132
    },
    {
      "text": "the Atlantic has produced deadly",
      "start": 10.132,
      "end": 11.452
    },
    {
      "text": "tsunamis before.",
      "start": 11.452,
      "end": 12.433
    },
    {
      "text": "In nineteen twenty-nine,",
      "start": 12.473,
      "end": 13.692
    },
    {
      "text": "a magnitude seven point two earthquake",
      "start": 13.692,
      "end": 15.688
    },
    {
      "text": "struck off Newfoundland.",
      "start": 15.688,
      "end": 16.689
    },
    {
      "text": "It triggered a massive underwater landslide.",
      "start": 16.729,
      "end": 18.78
    },
    {
      "text": "The tsunami killed twenty-eight people.",
      "start": 18.82,
      "end": 20.803
    },
    {
      "text": "Its waves were detected as far south",
      "start": 20.843,
      "end": 22.848
    },
    {
      "text": "as South Carolina.",
      "start": 22.848,
      "end": 23.888
    },
    {
      "text": "But what about New York?",
      "start": 24.288,
      "end": 25.297
    },
    {
      "text": "Scientists rate the Atlantic coast’s tsunami",
      "start": 25.647,
      "end": 27.917
    },
    {
      "text": "hazard as low.",
      "start": 27.917,
      "end": 28.913
    },
    {
      "text": "But not zero.",
      "start": 28.974,
      "end": 29.741
    },
    {
      "text": "And that famous mega-tsunami theory",
      "start": 29.781,
      "end": 31.743
    },
    {
      "text": "involving a collapsing volcano in the",
      "start": 31.743,
      "end": 33.625
    },
    {
      "text": "Canary Islands?",
      "start": 33.625,
      "end": 34.471
    },
    {
      "text": "USGS scientists say that nightmare scenario",
      "start": 34.511,
      "end": 36.942
    },
    {
      "text": "doesn’t hold up.",
      "start": 36.942,
      "end": 37.713
    },
    {
      "text": "So, could a tsunami reach New York?",
      "start": 38.113,
      "end": 39.837
    },
    {
      "text": "Yes.",
      "start": 39.919,
      "end": 40.315
    },
    {
      "text": "Could a monster wave wipe out Manhattan?",
      "start": 40.615,
      "end": 42.518
    },
    {
      "text": "That’s not a credible expected scenario.",
      "start": 42.572,
      "end": 44.429
    },
    {
      "text": "Myth or fact?",
      "start": 44.829,
      "end": 45.811
    },
    {
      "text": "The threat is real.",
      "start": 45.886,
      "end": 46.59
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hollywood disaster is not.",
      "start": 46.655,
      "end": 48.001
    }
  ],
  "narrationStart": 0.2,
  "narrationEnd": 48.001,
